    "title": "📘 Session 45 — In-class Activity: AI-Supported Fact-Checking and Editorial Response|||📘 Buổi 45 — In-class Activity: AI-Supported Fact-Checking and Editorial Response",
    "slug": "wda201-flm-b045",
    "type": "DOCUMENT",
    "isFreePreview": false,
    "description": "Buổi 45 theo syllabus FLM.",
    "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">WDA201 · Chapter 10 · Session 45</span>\n<h2>Session 45 — In-class Activity: AI-Supported Fact-Checking and Editorial Response</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM syllabus 14060 · session plan</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">WDA201 · Chương 10 · Buổi 45</span>\n<h2>Buổi 45 — In-class Activity: AI-Supported Fact-Checking and Editorial Response</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: syllabus FLM 14060 · kế hoạch buổi</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Type</span><span class=\"v\">Offline</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">LO</span><span class=\"v\">CLO3, CLO4</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">ITU</span><span class=\"v\">U</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Slides in this lesson</span><span class=\"v\">none from FLM</span></div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Hình thức</span><span class=\"v\">Offline</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">LO</span><span class=\"v\">CLO3, CLO4</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">ITU</span><span class=\"v\">U</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Slide trong bài</span><span class=\"v\">FLM không có</span></div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>What this session covers (FLM, verbatim)</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nội dung buổi học (FLM, nguyên văn)</h3></div>\n<p>In-class Activity: AI-Supported Fact-Checking and Editorial Response<br><br>Students will be provided with two short online texts (e.g., news posts, blog excerpts, or social media updates), one containing reliable information and one containing misinformation.<br><br>Using an AI tool, students must:<br><br>- Analyze the texts and identify factual inaccuracies, biased language, or credibility issues.<br><br>- Verify the information using AI fact-checking prompts and cross-referencing suggested sources.<br><br>- Write a short editorial response (200–250 words) that corrects the misinformation, explains the risks it poses to public trust, and demonstrates professional PR writing style.<br><br>- Submit both the AI analysis outputs and the final editorial response.</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Materials to read</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Tài liệu cần đọc</h3></div>\n<p>Textbook, PPT presentation, and other resources if has</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Student's tasks</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nhiệm vụ sinh viên</h3></div>\n<p>Use AI tools responsibly to detect and analyze misinformation.<br><br>Apply critical thinking to evaluate AI outputs and verify credibility.<br><br>Write a professional editorial response that addresses misinformation while maintaining clarity, ethics, and credibility.<br><br>Submit required deliverables on time.</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Detailed lecture and 🎬 video for this session: coming later. For now follow the slides, the materials and the tasks above.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Bài giảng chi tiết và 🎬 video cho buổi này: sẽ bổ sung sau. Trước mắt học theo slide, tài liệu và nhiệm vụ ở trên.</div></div>"
